1
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:33,500
Has James Bond finally met his match?

2
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:01,000
A View to a Kill is a adventure, action, thriller film directed by John Glen.

3
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:28,500
A newly-developed microchip designed by Zorin Industries for the British Government that can survive the
electromagnetic radiation caused by a nuclear explosion has landed in the hands of the KGB.

4
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:56,000
James Bond must find out how and why.

5
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:23,500
His suspicions soon lead him to big industry leader Max Zorin who forms a plan to destroy his only
competition in Silicon Valley by triggering a massive earthquake in the San Francisco Bay.

6
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:51,000
James Bond, played by Roger Moore.

7
00:38:12,500 --> 00:38:18,500
Stacey Sutton, played by Tanya Roberts.

8
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Max Zorin, played by Christopher Walken.

9
00:49:07,500 --> 00:49:13,500
May Day, played by Grace Jones.

10
00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:41,000
Tibbett, played by Patrick Macnee.

11
01:00:02,500 --> 01:00:08,500
Scarpine, played by Patrick Bauchau.

12
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:36,000
A View to a Kill is a 1985 spy film, the fourteenth in the James Bond series produced by Eon Productions,
and the seventh and final appearance of Roger Moore as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.

13
01:10:57,500 --> 01:11:03,500
Although the title is adapted from Ian Fleming's 1960 short story "From a
View to a Kill", the film has an entirely original screenplay.

14
01:16:25,000 --> 01:16:31,000
In A View to a Kill, Bond is pitted against Max Zorin (played by Christopher
Walken), who plans to destroy California's Silicon Valley.

15
01:21:52,500 --> 01:21:58,500
The film was produced by Albert R.

16
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:26,000
Broccoli and Michael G.

17
01:32:47,500 --> 01:32:53,500
Wilson, who also wrote the screenplay with Richard Maibaum.

18
01:38:15,000 --> 01:38:21,000
It was the third James Bond film to be directed by John Glen, and
the last to feature Lois Maxwell as Miss Moneypenny.

19
01:43:42,500 --> 01:43:48,500
Despite receiving negative reviews from critics, who criticised the ageing Moore's
performance, and Moore's own dislike of the film, it was a commercial success.

20
01:49:10,000 --> 01:49:16,000
The Duran Duran theme song "A View to a Kill" performed well in the charts, becoming the only Bond theme song to
reach number one on the Billboard Hot 100 and earning a Golden Globe nomination for Best Song.

21
01:54:37,500 --> 01:54:43,500
The film was followed by The Living Daylights in
1987, with Timothy Dalton playing Bond.

22
02:00:05,000 --> 02:00:11,000
The film explores themes of london, england,
helicopter, fire, drug abuse, france.

23
02:05:32,500 --> 02:05:38,500
The tone is intense.
